{"id": "bc5c8f1f-a2af-45e0-b039-e25e2b330fac", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll audit your SageMaker notebook instances and Studio domains for two things: internet exposure and encryption at rest. I'll cover the agent space account and any associated accounts, across the regions where SageMaker resources exist. The audit is read-only.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_U9vlVJPrsqGXMuLYrdMbTr", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "sagemaker-exposure-encryption-audit", "agent_type": "generic", "prompt": "{
  "task": "Run a READ-ONLY security audit of Amazon SageMaker notebook instances and SageMaker domains (Studio) for (1) internet exposure and (2) encryption at rest. Do not attempt any mutating operation.",
  "context": "User asked: 'Audit our SageMaker notebooks and domains for internet exposure and encryption at rest'. Agent space account is 012345678901_1 (region us-east-1, space ID 108b86bc-f94d-428a-a43a-ffe3d383e327). Use list_associations to find all associated AWS accounts and audit each one that is accessible. Enumerate every region where SageMaker is available (try all enabled regions; skip regions that error with access/opt-in issues and note them). Return a concise, severity-rated findings report.",
  "resources": ["SageMaker notebook instances (list_notebook_instances / describe_notebook_instance)", "SageMaker domains (list_domains / describe_domain)", "User profiles and spaces (list_user_profiles / describe_user_profile, list_spaces) where relevant", "Notebook instance lifecycle configs only if relevant", "Related VPC subnets, route tables, security groups, VPC endpoints where needed to judge exposure"],
  "timeframe": "Current state (point-in-time as of 2026-11-14T02:36:45Z)",
  "criteria": "INTERNET EXPOSURE - Notebook instances: DirectInternetAccess = Enabled (vs Disabled); whether in a VPC (SubnetId set) and whether subnet routes to an IGW or NAT; security groups with 0.0.0.0/0 or ::/0 ingress; RootAccess enabled. Domains: AppNetworkAccessType (PublicInternetOnly vs VpcOnly), whether subnets are public, security groups open to 0.0.0.0/0, presence of VPC endpoints for sagemaker api/runtime/studio, S3 etc. when VpcOnly. ENCRYPTION AT REST - Notebook instances: KmsKeyId set (customer-managed KMS key for the ML storage volume) vs none; note whether key is AWS-managed or customer-managed where determinable. Domains: KmsKeyId (EFS home directory encryption) is customer-managed or default; also check domain default space/user settings for any S3 output/ studio artifact KMS settings if present. Flag each resource as pass / warning / fail per dimension. Report: totals per account/region, a table of every non-compliant resource (name, account, region, issue, severity), a list of compliant resources count, any regions/accounts that could not be checked, and brief remediation guidance (note that notebook instance DirectInternetAccess/KMS settings and domain network type/KMS key generally cannot be changed in place and require recreation - verify via docs if unsure). Keep the report concise."
}", "preloaded_skills": ["discovering-topology", "verifying-with-docs"]}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Audit SageMaker notebooks and domains for exposure and encryption"}], "created_at": null}

